From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ballpad Native Port <ballpad-native@localhost>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:15:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] port: bound the frame burst to STRIKERS_CAPTURE_FROM/TO

STRIKERS_CAPTURE_EVERY writes a file every N frames from frame 0, which
makes a dense (EVERY=1) burst around one transition unusable: it would
write a file for every frame of the whole run.  Add an inclusive frame
window so the burst can start and stop where the evidence is wanted.
Both default to 0, and TO=0 stays unbounded, so the existing behaviour
of EVERY alone is unchanged.

// PORT: diagnostics only; no game logic is touched.
---
 smstrikers-port/src/Game/main.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smstrikers-port/src/Game/main.cpp b/smstrikers-port/src/Game/main.cpp
index c408835..c3f3c3f 100644
--- a/smstrikers-port/src/Game/main.cpp
+++ b/smstrikers-port/src/Game/main.cpp
@@ -869,17 +869,25 @@ int main(int argc, char* argv[])
 
         PortMaybeRequestCapture();
         // PORT: STRIKERS_CAPTURE_EVERY, a shot every N frames, so a long run can be watched rather than sampled once.
+        // PORT: STRIKERS_CAPTURE_FROM / STRIKERS_CAPTURE_TO bound that to an inclusive frame window, so a dense
+        // burst (EVERY=1) can follow one transition without writing a file for every frame of the whole run.
         {
             static long s_everyN = -1;
+            static unsigned long s_from = 0;
+            static unsigned long s_to = 0;   // 0 means unbounded
             if (s_everyN < 0)
             {
                 const char* e = getenv("STRIKERS_CAPTURE_EVERY");
                 s_everyN = (e != NULL && *e != '\0') ? strtol(e, NULL, 10) : 0;
                 if (s_everyN < 0)
                     s_everyN = 0;
+                s_from = PortEnvU32("STRIKERS_CAPTURE_FROM", 0);
+                s_to = PortEnvU32("STRIKERS_CAPTURE_TO", 0);
             }
             if (s_everyN > 0 && s_portFrame > 0
-                && (s_portFrame % (unsigned long)s_everyN) == 0)
+                && (s_portFrame % (unsigned long)s_everyN) == 0
+                && s_portFrame >= s_from
+                && (s_to == 0 || s_portFrame <= s_to))
             {
                 PortRequestManualShot();
             }
